00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:08.110 align:start position:0%
EU ministers for transport will work to  reach a general approach on the two  proposals to make the European air  transport system more efficient and to  further develop the single European sky  initiative launched in 2004 the SES  initiative aims to improve the  competitiveness of the European air  transport sector it would help overcome  the current fragmentation of the air  space and optimize the use of air  traffic management capacity on rail  transport the council will seek a  general approach on a proposal to repeal  the current regulation on accounts of  railway undertakings which has become  obsolete the objective is to eliminate  inconsistencies in the EU legal order  reduce red tape and ensure equal  treatment of companies ministers will  also take stock of the progress of to  other proposals aimed at improving rail  services in the EU by means of market  opening and stronger governance a set of  conclusions on transport infrastructure  and the trans-european network will be  adopted these conclusions will  contribute to the midterm review of the  Europe 2020 growth strategy scheduled  for 2015 ministers wish to point out the  contribution of the transport  infrastructure sector to growth and jobs  creation finally ministers will be asked  to agree on a decision to authorize  Member States to become parties of the  International Convention on standards  for fishing vessel personnel this  convention is the first attempt to make  safety standards for crews of fishing  vessels mandatory worldwide
 

